xnu 0419: kern.sweet_gpu_wait: the fence waits by back-off or by the GPU's interrupt instead of 50 us sleeps

msm_wait() (WAIT_FENCE, CPU_PREP, GEM_CLOSE's fallback, clientClose) looked at the fence word every 50 us. On this
port delay() always sleeps (SweetCPU registers no powergate_latency, so ml_delay_should_spin() is false), so each look
is a timer interrupt and two context switches: ~20000 wakeups a second per thread waiting for a frame. Report 16
(§3.2, §5.3) measures backboardd's fence waiter as the first cause of idle entries of the A73 cluster (15-21 %, one
wakeup every 142-217 us, ~980-1480 a second), each one a possible preemption of the render thread.

kern.sweet_gpu_wait (boot-arg gpu_wait), 0 by default:
  0  as before.
  1  back-off: 50 us, doubling up to kern.sweet_gpu_wait_max_us (500), each sleep with an eighth of it as leeway
     (delay_for_interval_with_leeway, TIMEOUT_URGENCY_LEEWAY): ~22 wakeups for a 10 ms frame instead of ~200, and a
     fence seen at most the cap late.
  2  the GPU's interrupt, the way kgsl and drm-msm wait (a6xx_submit: CP_EVENT_WRITE CACHE_FLUSH_TS | IRQ;
     a6xx_irq: read RBBM_INT_0_STATUS, write it to RBBM_INT_CLEAR_CMD, retire on bit 20 CP_CACHE_FLUSH_TS):
     - every CACHE_FLUSH_TS the kernel emits (the msm submissions' and event()'s) carries bit 31 of dword 0 (IRQ);
     - RBBM_INT_0_MASK = bit 20 only;
     - the distributor routes SPI 177 (INTID 209, level high; DT kgsl_3d0_irq "interrupts = <0 0xb1 4>") to the CPU
       of MPIDR kern.sweet_gpu_irq_mpidr (boot-arg gpu_irq_mpidr; 0 = the first A53): IPRIORITYR 0xA0, ICFGR level,
       IROUTER, then ISENABLER. Not armed if GICD_IGROUPR says Group 0 (TrustZone's);
     - sleh_irq (SWEET) calls a new hook, sweet_spi_hook, for INTID >= 32 before the EOI; gpu_spi() clears the
       GPU's status (and reads it back so the clear lands before the EOI) and thread_wakeup()s the waiters and one
       registered listener (0420's frame queue);
     - a waiter asserts its wait, looks once more (clear_wait if the fence is already there), and blocks until the
       interrupt or kern.sweet_gpu_wait_irq_us (2000), the net for a lost interrupt (drm-msm's hangcheck retires a
       missed fence the same way, every 500 ms);
     - 64 interrupts in a row with nothing in RBBM_INT_0_STATUS turn the line off in the distributor and the waits
       fall back to the back-off ("broken" in the stats); a line that comes while not armed is turned off too.
  Mode 2 is armed when chosen (the boot-arg once the service is up, or the sysctl, under service_lock) and disarmed
  when 0 or 1 is: no IRQ bit in the ring, RBBM_INT_0_MASK 0, the line off and its pending state cleared.
  gpu_recover() writes the mask again after its reset (the reset clears it) and wakes every waiter.

This is the first device SPI the port takes: pe_fiq.c only sets up the redistributors and sleh_irq() only EOIs any
other INTID. The boot-arg gpu_irq (0337) still only decides whether the line is masked during the bring-up.

kern.sweet_gpu_irq_stats: interrupts (CACHE_FLUSH_TS, other bits, empty, stray, last status), waits woken by the
interrupt and by the net, arms, disarms, and gdiag's wait loops and waits. kern.sweet_gpu_wait_max_us,
kern.sweet_gpu_wait_irq_us and kern.sweet_gpu_irq_mpidr are read at each use or arming.

Expected [not measured]: with 2, wakeups of the fence waiter ~1 per frame (plus the net's), idle entries of the A73
cluster down by 15-21 %, commit -> done latency the same or lower. Protocol: dev-notes/investigacion/anexos/
16-despertares/02-parches.md.
